1
00:00:00,099 --> 00:00:01,959
Look along the top edge of a windshield and

2
00:00:01,979 --> 00:00:03,500
you'll find a black border that breaks into

3
00:00:03,559 --> 00:00:05,279
a scatter of dots before it fades out.

4
00:00:05,539 --> 00:00:07,460
That border is ceramic paint baked into the

5
00:00:07,539 --> 00:00:08,139
glass,

6
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:10,000
and it is covering the adhesive that holds

7
00:00:10,019 --> 00:00:11,259
the windshield onto the car.

8
00:00:11,639 --> 00:00:13,139
Sunlight would slowly cook that glue,

9
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:14,619
so the black band shields it.

10
00:00:14,839 --> 00:00:15,960
The dots are the clever part.

11
00:00:16,239 --> 00:00:18,239
Black glass heats faster than clear glass,

12
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:20,000
and a hard edge between the two would build

13
00:00:20,039 --> 00:00:21,340
enough stress to crack the pane,

14
00:00:21,579 --> 00:00:23,639
so the dots spread that change out gradually.
